<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Soekor's third oil shipment due in Cape Town.</title>
<headline>Soekor's third oil shipment due in Cape Town.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The third tanker load of crude oil from South Africa's first offshore well is due in Cape Town harbour on Monday, state oil firm Soekor said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Soekor manager John Burton told reporters the Oribi field off Mossel Bay had produced about 1.5 million barrels since coming on stream in May.</p>
<p>&quot;The infrastructure is performing very well,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Burton said the well was pumping at an average of about 20,000 barrels per day, as planned, but this could go up to 25,000 in the summer when weather conditions were expected to improve.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +2721 252238</p>
